    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0129" n="120" xml:id="pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/802: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-03T18:00:00+02:00">June 3, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1644. My 1641, June 3, 4 p.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d147-f1"/> I was requested to
                    call at the Foreign Office this morning by Ritter who stated that prompt orders
                    had been issued to the German naval units to prevent any molestations of the S.
                    S. <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi> and in amplification of his remarks
                    handed me a copy of the press communiqué transmitted in my telegram under
                    reference. He said that while he could not guarantee the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >bona fides</hi> of the story of a Franco-British plot to sink the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington</hi> as well as other American vessels the
                    information had been received from what the Foreign Office regarded as
                    trustworthy sources. He further asserted that according to German information
                    the alleged plot involved both the use of a time-bomb within the ship and a
                    torpedo attack from outside.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
